Falsifies `file_allocation_table::reader::verification::no_chain_walk_outlasts_the_volume`.

The defect: the walk's bound is off by one, so a looping table yields one cluster more than the
volume holds before the walk stops.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(yielded <= clusters)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/reader.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/reader.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/reader.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/reader.rs
@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@
             },
             _ => return None,
         };
-        if self.yielded >= clusters {
+        if self.yielded > clusters {
             return Some(Err(ChainError::TooLong));
         }
         self.yielded += 1;
